## Proposed Changes (Assuming Option A)

### 1. State Management & Rendering Performance
Refactor `useTaskStore` to normalize the state and prevent expensive O(N) re-renders when a single task updates.
- **Store Shape:** Change `tasks: Task[]` to `tasks: Record<string, Task>` and maintain a separate array of `taskIds: string[]` if ordering is needed at the store level (though `TaskList` handles sorting).
- **Date Caching:** Parse and cache dates during the Supabase fetch instead of running `new Date()` continuously inside the `TaskList` filter/sort cycle.

#### [MODIFY] [taskStore.ts](file:///c:/Users/asnir/Documents/Projects%20Website/3.Zoabi_Planner/src/store/taskStore.ts)
- Change state interface to use a dictionary for tasks.
- Update `loadAll`, `addTask`, `updateTask`, `deleteTask`, and `bulkAddTasks` to work with the normalized state.
- Update `TasksPage`, `TaskList`, and other consumers to map over `Object.values(tasks)`.

### 2. Backend Sync & Data Mutations (Optimistic UI)
Modify `toggleTaskCompletion` and `updateTask` to update the local UI state synchronously before waiting for the Supabase network response.
- Apply state changes immediately.
- Await the Supabase `update` call in a `try...catch` block.
- Roll back the state if the Supabase call fails.

#### [MODIFY] [taskStore.ts](file:///c:/Users/asnir/Documents/Projects%20Website/3.Zoabi_Planner/src/store/taskStore.ts)
- Rewrite mutation functions for true Optimistic UI.

### 3. UI/UX Polish & Animations (Framer Motion)
Introduce layout animations so tasks smoothly slide around when filtered, sorted, or completed.
- Wrap the main list in `<AnimatePresence mode="popLayout">`.
- Wrap each `TaskItem` inside `TaskList.tsx` with a `<motion.div layout>` component.
- Disable the `<Resizable>` component on mobile devices so tasks default to a 100% width card view.

